# =============================================================================
# ONE-HOP www → apex + trailing slash (FORCE)
# =============================================================================
# Netlify's automatic www→apex keeps the path as requested, then Pretty URLs
# adds a trailing slash on HTML directories. That is the 2-hop chain Google
# is following (www/path → apex/path → apex/path/).
#
# These absolute-host rules with 301! sit at the top so they override that
# default www hop and land on the canonical apex + slash URL in one 301.
# Netlify first-match-wins; more specific rules come first.
#
# Assets and extensioned files must NOT get a trailing slash.
# Existing Squarespace / legacy consolidations are kept below unchanged.

# --- Static assets: keep the path, do not add a slash ---------------------
https://www.launchlayer.uk/assets/*  https://launchlayer.uk/assets/:splat  301!

